# core.autocrlf cannot be relied on here: on the development machine a global
# `false` overrides a system `true`, so with the effective value `false` git
# normalises nothing on `add` and CRLF that reaches the working tree gets
# committed verbatim. Normalise every text file to LF in the repo and on
# checkout, regardless of platform or any per-machine autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hook scripts must keep LF line endings: session-start is parsed by bash
# (CRLF breaks it), and the polyglot run-hook.cmd is parsed by both cmd.exe
# and bash. Never let autocrlf rewrite them on checkout. Redundant under the
# wildcard above, but kept as documentation of a hard constraint that must
# survive any later loosening of the wildcard.
hooks/* text eol=lf
